## Max context rule
Never load more than:
- 1 primary route card
- 2 specialist cards
- core gates already loaded

## Route purity check
If the answer contains architecture, STAR, ROI, DGS, MMM, and governance all at once, it failed route purity.


## Runtime self-check emission (W5.1)
At the very end of every answer (after the closing sentence, on its own line),
append a single machine-readable trailer in this exact shape:

```
SELF_CHECK: route=<N> cards_loaded=[<primary>,<specialist1>,<specialist2>]
```

Rules:

- `route=<N>` is the route number you chose (1-9 per the list above).
- `cards_loaded` is the ordered list of card filenames actually pulled
  into the answer, primary first, specialists after. Never more than 3
  entries (the max-context rule above).
- No prose after the trailer. No markdown formatting on the trailer line.
- If you abstained from a live answer (non-q prefix), skip the trailer —
  the `ingested` reply has no route.

This trailer is parsed post-rehearsal by card 22 Learnings to bind the
route decision to its outcome. It is the audit contract for route purity.
